# Docker Environment Rules

## Dockerfile Location

- Dockerfile must exist at:

environment/Dockerfile

- Docker-related files should remain inside the environment/ directory

---

# Base Image Rules

- Every FROM image must use digest pinning

Required:

FROM image:tag@sha256:<digest>

Forbidden:

FROM image:latest

FROM image:tag

- Use sanctioned base images unless explicitly exempt

---

# Runtime Requirements

Final runtime image must include:

- tmux
- asciinema

These dependencies must exist inside the built image, not installed later.

---

# Apt Installation Rules

When installing packages:

- Use --no-install-recommends
- Clean apt cache in the same layer
- Avoid unnecessary packages

Preferred pattern:

RUN apt-get update \
 && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends <packages> \
 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

---

# Dependency Rules

Dependencies must be reproducible.

Requirements:

- Pin package versions exactly
- Lock dependencies where possible
- Avoid unpinned installs

Forbidden:

pip install numpy

npm install

Allowed:

numpy==1.26.4

npm ci

---

# Copy Rules

Do NOT copy:

- solution/
- tests/
- hidden verifier assets

Runtime images must only contain files needed for execution.

Use:

COPY . .

Avoid selective copying that accidentally leaks hidden files.

---

# Environment Size Rules

Requirements:

- environment/ total size <= 100MB
- Individual files <= 50MB

Non-trivial environments should include:

.dockerignore

---

# Testing Rules

Everything required by:

tests/test.sh

must already exist inside the image.

Forbidden:

- Runtime downloads
- Runtime package installs
- Verifier installing dependencies

---

# Docker Compose Rules

Requirements:

- Use compose version 3.8 or compatible
- Pin image digests for service images

Forbidden:

- privileged containers
- unsafe capabilities
- unpinned service images

Good:

image: postgres:15@sha256:<digest>

Bad:

image: postgres:latest

---

# Multi-Service Rules

If multiple services are required:

- Use docker-compose
- Explicitly define dependencies
- Keep services minimal
- Only include required containers

---

# Git Repository Rules

When cloning repositories:

- Clone fixed commits only

Forbidden:

git clone repo && use HEAD

Required:

git clone repo \
&& git checkout <commit>

Never allow environments that expose future commits.

---

# Environment Validation Checklist

Before finishing verify:

- Dockerfile builds successfully
- Runtime image contains tmux + asciinema
- Every image uses digest pinning
- Dependencies are reproducible
- Runtime does not install dependencies
- Hidden assets are not copied
- Compose configuration is safe
- Environment size limits are respected

If any check fails, fix the environment before completion.
